WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.068
Black voters were obviously key

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:05.939
to President Biden being elected in

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.674
2020 and polls have shown

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:09.075
that his support

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:12.312
among young black Americans has softened.

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:13.913
How worrying is that

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:14.681
or should that be

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.783
for the president's reelection prospects

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.588
Look, I think the lesson

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:24.290
is that no group with young voters,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.458
whether it's black voters,

00:00:25.458 --> 00:00:26.726
whether it's Latino voters,

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:27.894
whether it's women voters,

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:30.630
whether it's any voter wants to be frank

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.032
and you have to work on it

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.400
and you have to work on

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.468
it's still not just a few weeks

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.603
before the election.

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.304
I think the Biden campaign understands

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:40.640
that that is why he is at Howard

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.876
giving that speech today,

00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:46.112
because it's basically an admission

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:48.982
of the importance of that vote.

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.050
As you know,

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:51.151
the speeches,

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.452
the commencement speeches that a

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.721
president and Vice gives are

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:56.823
and are

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.291
curated and I think

00:00:58.291 --> 00:01:01.194
and this is a reason for that.

00:01:01.194 --> 00:01:02.729
And honor back to the Republican field

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:03.963
and what's happening in Iowa

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:04.664
this weekend.

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:05.498
We heard our

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:05.965
our colleague

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:06.566
Steve Caetano

00:01:06.566 --> 00:01:07.300
saying that

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.335
DeSantis does not appear

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.104
to be wanting to go after Trump

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:12.238
this weekend,

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:12.572
that he's

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:14.674
avoiding these direct attacks on Trump,

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:16.076
almost certainly

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.610
because he fears alienating

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:18.645
that that Trump base,

00:01:18.645 --> 00:01:19.779
our Republican base.

00:01:19.779 --> 00:01:22.782
What do you make of that strategy?

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:24.084
Look, Sanchez

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.418
is going to have to do something.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:26.252
I think he hasn't

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.887
come into the race before

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.322
because the legislative session

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:30.790
was going on in Florida.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.259
That legislative session ended last week,

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:34.727
and he's still signing

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:36.463
some of the bills that were passed.

00:01:36.463 --> 00:01:37.797
But I also think DeSantis

00:01:37.797 --> 00:01:38.531
has done himself

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:40.500
an enormous amount of harm

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:42.068
in this legislative session

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:44.137
and in the last few months in Florida,

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:45.171
he has shown himself

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.239
to be the type of person

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.874
who weaponize his government,

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:50.777
whether it's against a drag branch

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:53.213
or against Disneyworld.

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:54.781
And that is costing him.

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.182
Floridians don't like that.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.317
And I think the number

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:58.351
that's got to be worrying

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:58.985
DeSantis

00:01:58.985 --> 00:01:59.886
the most

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:02.188
is the fact that his support has dropped

00:02:02.489 --> 00:02:04.757
not just nationally,

00:02:04.991 --> 00:02:06.259
but in the state of Florida,

00:02:06.259 --> 00:02:07.760
where we see him most

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.662
and where we know him best.

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.964
And that is something

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.499
that should be of great concern to him.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.401
Scott, I want to get your thoughts

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:17.170
on the flip side of that.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:21.007
And President Trump focusing primarily

00:02:21.574 --> 00:02:22.542
on Ron DeSantis,

00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:23.209
despite the fact

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.712
that there are others in the field,

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:28.081
namely Nikki Haley, Asa Hutchinson.

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:31.251
What do you make of that tactic?

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:31.985
Well, I mean,

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:32.852
the reality is all

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:33.720
these other candidates

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:34.721
are virtually nowhere.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:35.555
If you look at the polling,

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:37.390
they're all in low single digits.

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.191
They just don't carry

00:02:38.191 --> 00:02:39.692
the same positive name I.D.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:41.427
And the Republican Party of the Santos.

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.196
He's the only one in double digits.

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:43.930
If Trump

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:44.764
a Trump thinks that,

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.533
he could go ahead and dispatch DeSantis.

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.368
Now, none of these other people

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:49.969
are ever going to be able to rise up

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.137
and consolidate

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:53.473
the entire Trump lane of the party,

00:02:53.473 --> 00:02:54.207
or at least the people

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:55.241
who want to do something else.

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:56.643
Maybe they don't dislike Trump,

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:57.210
but maybe they think

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.144
we need a new nominee.

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.913
So dispatching DeSantis

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:00.680
before he ever really

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.648
gets out of the gate

00:03:01.648 --> 00:03:03.816
which he is working very diligently

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.386
on, obviously is priority one for Trump.

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:07.487
And there's some evidence

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:08.421
that it's working at the moment.

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:09.556
But I wouldn't count out DeSantis.

00:03:09.556 --> 00:03:09.889
There's a lot

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:10.924
a lot of runway left in the race.

